    "description": "John P. Koehler\nBlown Glass Cattail Sculpture\nArt Glass, Agate, and Burl Wood\n10\" x 4\" x 5\"\nSigned and dated 1992 on base\nThis intricate mixed media sculpture by artist John P. Koehler captures a stylized natural scene through a sophisticated combination of organic and artisanal materials. The work features hand-blown glass cattails accented with gold-tone luster and delicate clear glass reeds, all emerging from a base crafted from natural burl wood and polished agate geode slices. The composition reflects the studio glass movement of the late 20th century, emphasizing the contrast between the translucent, fragile nature of glass and the raw, earthy textures of stone and wood.\nFeatures two distinct gold-flecked blown glass cattails and multiple slender glass reeds\nBase constructed from a natural burl wood segment integrated with polished agate slices\nHand-signed and dated \"7-1992\" by the artist on the underside\nCondition:\nExcellent vintage condition. The glass elements are free of chips, cracks, or repairs. The burl wood and agate base are structurally sound with all components securely mounted. The signature on the underside remains clear and legible, and the four protective felt pads are present.\nThank you for all of your support!",
